ound 5mm.\n\nThe \"dot\" is bright next to a dark ring (bronchus). This has characteristics of a \"signet ring\" sign. The bright dot is the pulmonary artery branch.\n\nLet's do a final check.\n\n*   **Slice 1-7:** The bright dot, and not a vessel, is the focal point.\n*   **Slice 8 & 9:** The dot expands into a branching structure.\n\nTherefore, the structure is a vessel.\n\nHere's my final breakdown:\n\n**Vessel**\n\n*   **Reasoning:** The central round opacity elongates into a tubular, branching structure in the inferior slices, confirming it is a blood vessel.\n*   **Diameter:** The FOV is 64mm. The dot is roughly 1/12th of the image width. 64/12 ≈ 5.3 mm, let's estimate 5 mm.\n\nLet's double-check again...\n*   **Slice 1-7:** dot\n*   **Slice 8:** dot connects to a line to the right.\n*   **Slice 9:** line continues.\n\nYes, it's a vessel.\n**Reasoning:** The structure elongates into a tubular shape and branches in the inferior slices.\n**Diameter:** ~5 mm"
